  "notes": "Boot ft_l5 from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released) and PinMAME's built-in mechanisms disabled (the drop-target and reel mechs would overwrite 48 and 37/38), navigate the service menu to T.1 SWITCH EDGES and start it, then drive each public level of switch 41 (Captive Ball, an ordinary switch), 112 (the Fliptronic lower-right flipper-button opto, which PinMAME normalizes through its WPC_FLIPPERS column complement; the ROM fires the right flipper and PinMAME's end-of-stroke simulation then raises the watched 111), 47/48 (Ball Popper and Drop Target, printed as ordinary microswitches and outside ftGameData's inverted-switch mask) and 37/38 (the Reel 1/Reel 2 optos, which that mask inverts: index 3 = 0xc0 is matrix column 3, rows 7-8 under wpc_sw2m) separately, holding each level for 2 s. 37 and 38 start at public 0 and are returned to 1 so both edges are seen. The ROM's top display line names a switch while it reads it as active, so the edge that brings the name up shows which public level the ROM treats as active.",
